This is the potential for aspirin, described in J. Chem. Theory Comput. (2024) 20: 3008-3018
(https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.4c00054). Specifically, the fit labeled as "PES4"

The folder `coeff` contains the fitting coefficients.

`bemsa_aspirin.f90` contains the permutationally invariant polynomials for this molecule. This
file may take a long time to compile.

`pes_shell.f90` contains essential functions and subroutines to call this potential.

An example `testpot.f90` is given to show how to initialize and then call the PES to calculate
the potential energy and gradient, using Cartesian coordinate as input

To compile, modify the Makefile and use it to compile the program. To run the test,
./testpot.x GMgeom.xyz
The output is written to GMgeom.out
